# POSITIVE FIXTURE — this file MUST conform, on BOTH legs. See tests/test_arc_manifest.py.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix prog: <https://w3id.org/iladub/progress#> .

# Decision 6: UNKNOWN IS NOT ZERO. A rung that declares no criteria renders `?` on the
# strip — never an empty bar, never 0/0 — and it is deliberately NOT a refusal.
#
# This claim used to be asserted of the live tests/arc-manifest.ttl while that file was a
# seed with five rungs and no criteria. It stopped being assertable there the moment the
# loop started authoring criteria, and it will be unassertable there for good once all five
# rungs are populated. So the claim moved here, where it is permanent and independent of how
# full the real manifest is (CLAUDE.md § Serialization: every shape ships with a worked
# example that conforms).
prog:rung:dec a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "dec" ;
    rdfs:label "decidability, the context graph" .
